# Environment variables for FinBuddy
# Local development: copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values.
# Production: set the same variables in Vercel (Settings -> Environment Variables),
# then redeploy. See README "Changing settings in Vercel" for a click-by-click guide.
#
# Secrets are server-side only. NEVER prefix any of these with NEXT_PUBLIC_ —
# that embeds the value in the public JavaScript bundle.

## ============ LLM PROVIDERS ============
## At least ONE of the four keys below must be set, or the app refuses to boot.
## Which one actually answers a request is decided by DEFAULT_VENDOR below,
## falling back through PROVIDER_FALLBACK_ORDER (config.ts) to whichever keys
## exist. This deployment runs on Google (Gemini) by default; the others stay
## available to switch to any time with no code change.

## Google (Gemini) — the configured default vendor, and the only provider here
## with a genuine free tier: an AI Studio key needs no payment details.
## Note the free tier limits both requests/minute AND requests/day, so a busy
## demo can exhaust it; keep a second provider's key set as a fallback.
## Get it at: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

## Anthropic (Claude) — optional switchable provider.
## Get it at: https://console.anthropic.com
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

## OpenAI — needed for OpenAI chat models, and for MODERATION_PROVIDER=openai.
## Get it at: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

## Fireworks — only for the open-source models (DeepSeek, Kimi) in the catalog.
FIREWORKS_API_KEY=

## ============ MODEL SELECTION ============
## These override the fallbacks in config.ts, so changing the model on a
## deployed app is a Vercel dashboard edit + redeploy — no code change, no
## commit, no push. Leave them unset to use the config.ts values.
##
## An unrecognised vendor or an empty value is ignored in favour of the
## fallback, so a typo here degrades to "keeps working", never to a dead site.

## Which provider answers chat. One of: google | anthropic | openai | fireworks
## Its API key above must be set, or the app falls back to one that is.
# DEFAULT_VENDOR=google

## Which model, within that vendor. Must be listed for the vendor in
## lib/ai/providers.ts, or that vendor's own default is used instead.
##   google     -> gemini-2.5-flash | gemini-3.5-flash | gemini-3.8-flash | gemini-2.5-pro
##   anthropic  -> claude-haiku-4-5 | claude-sonnet-4-6 | claude-sonnet-5
##   openai     -> gpt-5.6-luna | gpt-5.4-mini | gpt-5.6-terra
## NOTE: gemini-3.5-flash's FREE tier is only 20 requests PER DAY and will
## break every chat once exhausted. Prefer gemini-2.5-flash on a free key.
# DEFAULT_MODEL_ID=gemini-2.5-flash

## Background work (moderation classifier, compaction summaries). Kept separate
## from the chat model on purpose — this should stay cheap and predictable.
# UTILITY_VENDOR=google
# UTILITY_MODEL_ID=gemini-2.5-flash

## In-app model picker (dropdown in the header).
## When true, visitors can pick any model this deployment can serve. The server
## re-validates the choice, so nothing unservable can be selected — but on a
## PUBLIC site with a PAID key set, any visitor can spend it. Set to false to
## hide the dropdown and pin everyone to DEFAULT_VENDOR/DEFAULT_MODEL_ID.
# ENABLE_MODEL_PICKER=true

## ============ RETRIEVAL & SEARCH ============

## Pinecone — the knowledge base (vector search).
## REQUIRED unless ENABLE_VECTOR_SEARCH=false; the app fails loudly at startup
## rather than silently answering without citations.
## The index name itself is set in config.ts (PINECONE_INDEX_NAME).
## Get it at: https://app.pinecone.io
PINECONE_API_KEY=

## Exa — web search. REQUIRED unless ENABLE_WEB_SEARCH=false.
## Get it at: https://dashboard.exa.ai
EXA_API_KEY=

## ============ RATE LIMITING (optional but recommended) ============

## Shared rate-limit store. WITHOUT these, the limiter counts requests in each
## serverless instance's own memory — so with N warm instances on Vercel the
## real ceiling is RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS x N, and a cold start resets a
## client's history. With them, one shared counter holds across instances and
## restarts, and the configured limit is the actual limit.
## Free tier, no npm package needed (proxy.ts calls the REST API directly).
## Create a database at https://console.upstash.com -> Redis -> REST API.
## Set BOTH or neither.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

## ============ SECURITY (optional) ============

## Secret used to sign conversation summaries (HMAC) so clients cannot forge
## them. If unset, a key is derived from whichever provider API key is present.
## Set it explicitly in production so the signature does not change when you
## rotate a provider key. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# SUMMARY_HMAC_SECRET=

## Token that unlocks the detailed /api/health dependency checks in production
## (send as "Authorization: Bearer <token>"). If unset, /api/health returns
## only {"status":"ok"} in production. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# HEALTH_CHECK_TOKEN=

## ============ FEATURE SWITCHES ============
## These turn features on or off without any code change.
## If a switch is not set, its default applies. Remove the leading # to use one.

## Knowledge base on/off. Default: enabled.
## Set to false to disconnect Pinecone entirely — the bot then answers from
## general knowledge (plus web search, if enabled). PINECONE_API_KEY not needed.
# ENABLE_VECTOR_SEARCH=false

## Web search on/off. Default: enabled.
## Set to false to disable Exa web search. EXA_API_KEY not needed.
# ENABLE_WEB_SEARCH=false

## Which service safety-checks user messages before the chat model sees them.
## Default: llm (a fast check by the utility model configured in config.ts).
##   llm    = LLM classifier — runs on whichever vendor is configured, so this
##            works on a Gemini-only or Anthropic-only deployment alike
##   openai = OpenAI's dedicated moderation API (requires OPENAI_API_KEY)
##   off    = no safety check (system prompt guardrails only)
# MODERATION_PROVIDER=llm
